{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794338458,"nonce":"7Q45RXBR9NQ5KxEQ1tzU8HQPezw=","message":"Correction to the layer effect comment: the 28 outputs of the inline WGSL are kept as per-machine goldens in .blinc/snapshots/blinc_gpu/\u003cos\u003e (untracked, like the recorder's), not as committed fixtures. A new gitignore rule, **/fixtures/**/*.png, would have kept committed PNGs out of the repository anyway, and committed images would be fragile across adapters. The tests skip when a machine has no goldens and compare when it has (BLINC_SNAPSHOT=bless records them), so on CI these seven shaders are guarded only by the pixel-parity evidence gathered before the swap.","files":null}]}